{"key":"enterprise/T1578.001","id":"T1578.001","name":"Create Snapshot","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1578","tactics":["defense-impairment"],"platforms":["IaaS"],"environments":["cloud"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"An adversary may create a snapshot or data backup within a cloud account to evade defenses. A snapshot is a point-in-time copy of an existing cloud compute component such as a virtual machine (VM), virtual hard drive, or volume. An adversary may leverage permissions to create a snapshot in order to bypass restrictions that prevent access to existing compute service infrastructure, unlike in Revert Cloud Instance where an adversary may revert to…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1578/001","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--ed2e45f9-d338-4eb2-8ce5-3a2e03323bc1","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.723Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0057","name":"Snapshot Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0057","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3da222e6-53f3-451c-a239-0b405c009432","page":"telemetry/DC0057/"},{"id":"DC0062","name":"Snapshot Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0062","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--8bc66f94-54a9-4be4-bdd1-fe90df643774","page":"telemetry/DC0062/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0423","name":"Detection Strategy for Modify Cloud Compute Infrastructure: Create Snapshot","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0423","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--160f132d-626e-412a-ae16-df265670c196","relationship_id":"relationship--2e8e1e84-69c7-4302-abb9-3ae279f485c7"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1187","name":"Analytic 1187","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0423#AN1187","guidance":"Detection focuses on correlating snapshot creation events with subsequent instance creation and mounting activities. From a defender perspective, suspic